 "capsule": "Rostov-Suzdal grew out of lands assigned to Vsevolod Yaroslavich's line from 1054 and was confirmed to Vladimir Monomakh's family at the Council of Lyubech in 1097; his son Yuri Dolgoruky moved its seat to Suzdal in 1125 and founded Moscow in 1147 while building up the principality's cities and boyar class. After the senior line shifted its capital to Vladimir in 1157, a separate Rostov branch under Konstantin Vsevolodovich (from 1207) and his son Vasilko continued to rule Rostov and Yaroslavl as an appanage, ending when Vasilko was killed refusing submission to Batu Khan's Mongols after the Battle of the Sit River in 1238.",
